<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian manufacturing output prices fall.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian manufacturing output prices fall.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's manufacturing output prices fell 0.2 percent in April to be 0.6 percent up on the year, the Australian Bureau of Statistics reported on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Prices fell 0.1 percent in March for a 0.7 percent year-on-year rise.</p>
<p>Manufacturing output prices (base 1988/89):</p>
<p>			 Index     mth/mth pct    yr/yr pct</p>
<p>    April	    122.0     -0.2	     +0.6</p>
<p>March	    122.2     -0.1	     +0.7</p>
<p>    April 1996     121.3     -0.1	     +1.2</p>
<p>Note - The bureau said price reductions for refined petroleum products were the main contributors to the decrease in the index.  </p>
<p>It said price rises for processed seafoods, basic metals and motor vehicles partly offset the overall drop.</p>
<p>-- Canberra bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
